{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794910622,"nonce":"6Cpx1BAMItPW0v0uhFfqZmkn3qw=","message":"Implemented locally. hxn plugins discovers installed registrations without executing them; hxn \u003cnamespace\u003e dispatches commands without requiring a Cargo project. package.metadata.hxn.cli is carried into haxelib.json by hxn package. Tools under sources/ ship automatically; optional files entries carry binary assets with executable permissions preserved. CI haxelib assembly retains this content, so a separate plugin installation is unnecessary.\n\nThe version-1 JSON subprocess protocol uses argv entries and {root} expansion, never a shell command. Hooks cover before-check, before/after-build, before/after-run and before/after-package. Only source and selected haxe-flags libraries activate hooks, in deterministic order. The source registration overrides its installed copy. Built-in namespaces, duplicates, unsupported versions, malformed replies and unknown phases fail explicitly; failures identify the provider/phase. Build replies can contribute constrained Haxe arguments and page files. Plugin defines also reach CPPIA script compilation.\n\nhxn-window is the first integration: installed window doctor and window check commands, plus source hooks to generate its browser modules. Its packaged checks work without Rust or a source checkout. Current-design CLI, packaging, design and convention docs are updated, along with hxn, hxn-window and hxn-gpu skills and their site mirrors.\n\nValidation: cargo test --workspace, cargo fmt and workspace all-target clippy passed. Protocol tests exercise real subprocess argv/JSON (including spaces and metacharacters), statuses, invalid metadata/replies and binary asset packaging. CLI integration covers lifecycle ordering, selection/activation, hook failures, Haxe defines, package metadata/tools/assets, installed command discovery outside Cargo and exit-status propagation. All 51 local runtime matrix cases passed, spanning counter/generated adapters, CLI, examples, C import and web tests; threaded cases were repeated. Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm and Emscripten are covered. All four mobile configurations (iOS simulator and Android emulator, each cpp and hl/Ash) passed. Stock HashLink and Windows CI were unavailable locally. ABI/future crates were unchanged, so Miri was not run. Additional Linux source-upload validation is pending explicit authorization after automatic approval review rejected that optional upload.\n\nNo commits, pushes or publications made. Keep open for the coordinated CLI/haxelib release and consumer dependency/version updates; the current released v0.3.6 CLI cannot dispatch these new extensions.","files":null}]}